From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pppd clear pppdb after tdb close

---
pppd: clear pppdb after tdb_close() in ppp_safe_fork() child

Backport of upstream ppp commit 26093eeea8; the change is byte-identical
to upstream, only the context line numbers differ.

ppp_safe_fork() closes the inherited TDB handle in the child so that a
script cannot disturb the parent's database, but it leaves the global
`pppdb' pointer pointing at the freed tdb_context.

run_program() keeps running in that child and calls
ppp_script_setenv("PPP_SCRIPT_INSTANCE", ...) before fexecve(). That call
was added by e87ddf0085c6 for 2.5.4 and is what makes the stale pointer
reachable again: ppp_script_setenv() sees pppdb != NULL and ends up in
update_db_entry() -> tdb_store() -> tdb_lock() on the freed context.

    ldr  w1, [x1, x22]        ; x22 = (list + 1) * 8
                              ; x1  = tdb->locked  (already freed by
                              ;       tdb_close() -> SAFE_FREE())

The new environment string is malloc()ed immediately afterwards, so it
frequently reuses the freed chunk and the outcome depends on heap
layout. Observed on 2.5.4 + PPPoE (airoha/an7581): every script child
dies, reproducibly

    pppd: pppd: potentially unexpected fatal signal 11.
    pc : 0045434e4154534e          <- ASCII "NSTANCE\0": the recycled
                                      chunk now holds the
                                      "PPP_SCRIPT_INSTANCE" string
    Child process /lib/netifd/ppp-up (pid N) terminated with signal 11

The parent only logs the failure and carries on, so ip-up, ip-down and
ppp6-up are silently skipped. With netifd that means
/lib/netifd/ppp-up never runs, notify_proto is never called and the WAN
default route is never installed -- while PPPoE/LCP/IPCP themselves
complete fine and the data plane works.

Only builds with --enable-multilink (PPP_WITH_TDB) are affected; that is
what the ppp-multilink package variant selects.

Upstream: 26093eeea8 ("pppd: Clear pppdb after tdb_close() in ppp_safe_fork()")
          Author: Adam Zegarek <keragez@gmail.com>
Fixes:    e87ddf0085c6 ("run_program: Export the name of the script via PPP_SCRIPT_INSTANCE")
Note:     droppable once ppp is bumped past 2.5.4 -- as of v2.5.4 the fix
          exists only on upstream master, no release contains it.

--- a/pppd/main.c
+++ b/pppd/main.c
@@ -1755,8 +1755,10 @@
 	/* Executing in the child */
 	ppp_sys_close();
 #ifdef PPP_WITH_TDB
-	if (pppdb != NULL)
+	if (pppdb != NULL) {
 		tdb_close(pppdb);
+		pppdb = NULL;	/* tdb_close() can't null the caller's pointer */
+	}
 #endif
 
 	/* make sure infd, outfd and errfd won't get tromped on below */
